.PRO.9.11.010"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.11.010", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PRO.9.11.a011", "note": "Construct noun with a supplied *the*, rule 29.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.11.011"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.11.011", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PRO.9.11.a012", "note": "Rectum takes the *of*; discontinuous around the possessive under rule 25.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.11.012"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.11.012", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t014"], "target_head": "t014"}], "ref": "PRO.9.11", "review_notes": ["The second colon is a passive recasting of יוסיפו לך, which is why the ל has no English word of its own."], "source_edition": "ASV-alignment Hebrew projection", "target_edition": "ASV", "variant_decisions": []}
{"alignments": [{"id": "PRO.9.12.a001", "note": "אם takes the *If*.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a002", "note": "Subject pronoun and copular auxiliary with the verb, rule 17.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a003", "note": "Second finite verb, rule 17.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t005", "t006", "t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a004", "note": "Preposition.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a005", "note": "Suffix, rule 18.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a006", "note": "The ASV recasts this waw's clause as a conditional and writes a coordinator and a subordinator together at its left edge; both words are the one connective's rendering under rule 55, headed on the coordinator.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010", "t011"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a007", "note": "Rule 17.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t012", "t013"], "target_head": "t013"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a008", "note": "Preposition and its noun rendered by one English adverb; rule 30's one-rendering condition is met and the pair fuses, headed on the noun carrying the lexeme.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.12.008", "WLC.PRO.9.12.009"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.12.009", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PRO.9.12.a009", "note": "The ASV writes no separate pro