{"alignments": [{"id": "PRO.9.13.a001", "note": "Construct noun rendered as the English head with its supplied *the* under rule 29; the resumed subject *She* of the next colon is a further realization of this written noun and joins its discontinuous unit under rule 25. The competing reading marks that pronoun added under rule 20.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001", "t003", "t006"], "target_head": "t003"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a002", "note": "Rectum rendered attributively, rule 28. The margin's *Folly* was read and set aside, rule 38.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002"], "target_head": "t002"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a003", "note": "Participial predicate takes the construction-supplied copula, rule 20.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t004", "t005"], "target_head": "t005"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a004", "note": "Predicate noun with its copula, rule 20. The margin's literal gloss corroborates without deciding, rule 38.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007", "t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a005", "note": "Waw, rule 14.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a006", "note": "One English word carries both the negation and the indefinite quantifier; the two morphemes share one discontinuous unit headed on the negative, rule 35.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.006", "WLC.PRO.9.13.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PRO.9.13.a007", "note": "Finite verb.", "source": ["WLC.PRO.9.13.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PRO.9.13.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}], "ref": "PRO.9.13", "revie